      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional bodies derive their powers directly from the Constitution of India.",
        "Statutory bodies are established by an Act of Parliament or State Legislature.",
        "Executive bodies are created by a simple government resolution without legislative enactment.",
        "Constitutional amendments are required to alter the structure or powers of constitutional bodies."
      ],
      "id": "b1w3cju"
